    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grăvĕŏlens</span></b>  (also
		separately: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grave olens</span></b> ),
			entis, adj.
		gravis-, 1. oleo. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Strong - smelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">graveolentia centaurea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 270</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			a bad sense. <i>illsmelling</i>, <i>noisome</i>, <i>rank</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fauces graveolentis Averni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 201</span></i>
			; App. de Mundo, p. 74.</div>
